    "result_text": "The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires validating an E.164 telephone's national-number length against its country code, rejecting with 400 when wrong.\n\nI implemented this in `TelephoneE164.normalize` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/TelephoneE164.java`), the shared normalizer already used by `ValidateNewOwner` in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline. It already threw `InvalidTelephoneException` (\u2192 400 via `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler`) for the general 8\u201315 digit E.164 bound; I added a per-country national-length check on top of it:\n\n- A `NATIONAL_LENGTH` map (`LinkedHashMap`, longest-prefix-first) maps country code \u2192 required national digit count: `\"61\" \u2192 9`, `\"1\" \u2192 10`.\n- After the general length check, the normalized digit string is matched against the first country-code prefix; if the remaining national digits don't equal the required count, it throws `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\nOrdering `\"61\"` before `\"1\"` ensures a `+61` number isn't mis-matched as `+1` (a `+61` digit string starts with `6`, never conflicting with the `1` code).\n\nVerification:\n- New test `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` (`+61 123` \u2192 400) passes.\n- Full suite: `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green. Existing valid data stays valid \u2014 `uniqueTelephone()` (`04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 `+61` + 9 national digits) and the `+1` NANP seed data (10 national digits) both satisfy the new rule.",
